px;\"><strong>Brahmi (Centella asiatica):</strong>&nbsp;Brahmi improves nervous functions and helps to control anxiety and stress.</span></span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Amla (Emblica officinalis):</strong>&nbsp;The fruit is aphrodisiac, haemostatic, nutritive tonic and rejuvenative. It increases red blood cell count. Amalaki is one of the highest natural source of Vitamin C.</span></span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Sounth (Zingiber officinale):</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;Saunth stimulates peripheral circulation to the extremities resulting in a warming effect on the testicles and improved functioning of penile muscles.</span></span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Jaiphal (Myristica fragans):</strong>&nbsp;It acts as an aphrodisiac by stimulating the central nervous system and warming the loins.Jaiphal has a tranquilizing effect that helps to avert premature ejaculation.&nbsp;</span></span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Ashwagandha (Withania somnifera dunal.):</strong>Ashwagandha has been used for thousands of year to treat impotence, premature ejaculation, infertility, and erection disorders.</span></span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Kaunch Beej (Mucana puruita):</strong>&nbsp;High levels of L-dopa in Kaunch Beej has been found to promote fertility, sperm production, and also the penis size.</span></span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Shatawar (Asparagus racemosus):</strong>&nbsp;Shatavari is a rejuvenating herb that soothes the body to relieve stress, nurtures the reproductive system, 